# Shell scripts must stay LF -- a stray CR breaks bash outright, not just
# cosmetically. Found live: `tools/refuse_if_parked.sh` failed the
# QuStudio Tauri build on this machine with `$'\r': command not found`
# and `set: pipefail: invalid option name`, the exact symptoms of a CRLF
# shebang line. The committed blobs are already plain LF (checked via
# `git show HEAD:tools/refuse_if_parked.sh | file -`) -- the corruption
# was happening at CHECKOUT time, on Windows, with no `.gitattributes` to
# tell git these files must not be translated. 14 of 14 tools/*.sh
# scripts were affected in this exact checkout before this file existed.
*.sh text eol=lf
